      "message": "See commit message; this way Git doesn\u0027t get confused, thinking that `src/arch.rs` gets modified (which Rust requires us to re-introduce) while we are adding a new file (`src/arch/aarch64.rs`).\n\nInstead, using 2 commits makes it completely clear to Git that we\u0027re \"moving\" `arch.rs`. As a result, it will properly attribute the current history of `arch.rs` to the new `aarch64.rs` instead of the new `arch.rs`. In turn, this means diffs easier to review and rebasing changes to `arch.rs` should go smoothly (as Git will actually target `aarch64.rs`).",
